{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"d391337c-053d-4254-b19e-9e3182723c6d","title":"Ray diagram for a converging lens"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d391337c-053d-4254-b19e-9e3182723c6d","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A converging lens brings parallel rays toward its far focus. Place an object beyond twice the focal length? Here, exactly twice: at two F.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Converging lens: object at 2F"},{"op":"figure","id":"lensfig","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-5,5],"y":[-2.3,2.3],"axes":"none","equal_scale":true},"marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"axis","from":[-4.8,0],"to":[4.8,0],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"param","id":"lens","x":"0.2*cos(t)","y":"2*sin(t)","t":[0,6.283185307179586]},{"kind":"point","id":"center","at":[0,0],"label":"O"},{"kind":"point","id":"nearfocus","at":[-2,0],"label":"F"},{"kind":"point","id":"farfocus","at":[2,0],"label":"F"},{"kind":"point","id":"objecttip","at":[-4,1.5]},{"kind":"segment","id":"object","from":[-4,0],"to":{"at":"objecttip"},"arrow":true,"label":"object"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d391337c-053d-4254-b19e-9e3182723c6d","step":{"id":"s2","script":"From the object’s tip, draw a ray parallel to the axis. After the lens, it passes through the far focus.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"parallelray","on":"lensfig","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"lenshit","at":[0,1.5]},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"objecttip"},"to":{"at":"lenshit"},"arrow":true},{"kind":"segment","id":"refracted","from":{"at":"lenshit"},"to":[4.6,-1.95],"arrow":true}]},{"op":"text","id":"ruleone","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Parallel ray → far focus"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d391337c-053d-4254-b19e-9e3182723c6d","step":{"id":"s3","script":"A second ray passes straight through the optical center. The two outgoing rays meet below the axis on the far side.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"centralray","on":"lensfig","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"straight","from":{"at":"objecttip"},"to":[4.6,-1.725],"arrow":true},{"kind":"point","id":"imagetip","at":{"hit":["refracted","straight"]}}]},{"op":"text","id":"ruletwo","anchor":{"el":"ruleone","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Central ray → straight through"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Is the image upright or inverted, and real or virtual?","expected_gist":"Inverted and real: outgoing rays actually meet."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d391337c-053d-4254-b19e-9e3182723c6d","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Draw the image from the axis to that intersection. At two F, the image is real, inverted, and the same size as the object.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"finishimage","on":"lensfig","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":[4,0],"to":{"at":"imagetip"},"arrow":true,"label":"image"},{"kind":"text","at":[4,0.3],"text":"2F"},{"kind":"text","at":[-4,-0.3],"text":"2F"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"ruletwo","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"d_o=d_i=2f,\\qquad m=-\\frac{d_i}{d_o}=-1"},{"op":"text","id":"summary","anchor":{"el":"result","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Real • inverted • same size"}],"checkpoint":null}}
